We have;
$\int \frac{d x}{x^2\left(x^n+1\right)^{\frac{(n-1)}{n}}}=\int \frac{d x}{x^2 \cdot x^{n-1}\left(1+\frac{1}{x^n}\right)^{\frac{(n-1)}{n}}}=\int \frac{d x}{x^{n+1}\left(1+x^{-n}\right)^{\frac{(n-1)}{n}}}$
Put, $1+x^{-n}=t\therefore \quad-n x^{-n-1} d x=d t\Rightarrow \quad \frac{d x}{x^{n+1}}=\frac{-d t}{n}\Rightarrow \quad \int \frac{d x}{x^2\left(x^n+1\right)^{\frac{(n-1)}{n}}}=-\frac{1}{n} \int \frac{d t}{t^{\frac{(n-1)}{n}}}=-\frac{1}{n} \int t^{(1 / n)-1} d t=-\frac{1}{n} \cdot \frac{t^{\left(\frac{1}{n}-1+1\right)}}{\left(\frac{1}{n}-1+1\right)}+c=-t^{1 / n}+c=-\left(1+x^{-n}\right)^{\frac{1}{n}}+c$

We have,
$\begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{x(x+1)(x+2) \ldots(x+n)}= \frac{A_0}{x}+\frac{A_1}{x+1}+\ldots+ \\ & \frac{A_t}{x+r}+\ldots+\frac{A_n}{x+n}\end{aligned}\begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow \quad 1=A_0(x+1)(x+2) \ldots(x+n) \\ & +\ldots+A_r x(x+1)(x+2) \ldots(x+r-1)(x+r+1) \\ & \quad \ldots(x+n)+\ldots+A_n x(x+1) \ldots(x+n-1)\end{aligned}$
Putting $x=-r$, we get;
$\begin{array}{r}1=A_r(-r)(-r+1)(-r+2) \ldots(-3)(-2)(-1)(1)(2) \\ \ldots(n-r)\end{array}
$\begin{aligned} \Rightarrow 1=A_r(-1)^r\{r(r-1)(r-2) \ldots(3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1\} \\ (1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \ldots(n-r))\end{aligned}\Rightarrow \quad A_r=(-1)^r / r!(n-r)!

$\text { Let } \begin{aligned}
I & =\int \frac{2 d x}{\left(e^x+e^{-x}\right)^2}=\int \frac{2 d x}{e^{2 x}+e^{-2 x}+2} \\
& =\int \frac{2 e^{2 x} d x}{e^{4 x}+2 e^{2 x}+1}
\end{aligned}$
Put $\quad e^{2 x}=t\Rightarrow \quad 2 e^{2 x} d x=d t\begin{aligned} \therefore \quad I & =\int \frac{d t}{t^2+2 t+1}=\int \frac{d t}{(t+1)^2}=-\frac{1}{t+1}+c \\ & =-\frac{1}{e^{2 x}+1}=-\frac{e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}+c\end{aligned}$
